          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Analyse and interpret each of the observations you made. Share appropriate summary/conclusion statements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.486,
            0.847,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Punjab, the monthly maximum temperature increases from January to June, reaching a high of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 8 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Then, it reduces to just under "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in July, stays mostly flat till September, and then falls continuously till December, reaching about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 3 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " January has the lowest among the monthly maximum temperature of about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 9 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.583,
            0.847,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kerala’s trend is different — it stays mostly flat throughout the year. The peak is around "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 3 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in April and the lowest point is around "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 9 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in July. Notice that the monthly maximum temperatures in"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.639,
            0.66,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kerala are similar both in summer and winter!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.662,
            0.656,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In short, the temperature in Punjab varies more, reaching colder and warmer temperatures than in Kerala."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.722,
            0.712,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can trigger questions in different directions, some of which can be answered using data. Here are some directions to think about —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.784,
            0.722,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why are the trends so distinct in these two states? What factors determine a region’s temperature?"
            }
          ]
        },
